Port: files dropped from other applications, as WPEView::file-drag.

WPE has no drop target: a file dragged from a file manager over a WPE
window is refused. This adds a signal on WPEView,

  file-drag (phase, x, y, uris)    phase: WPE_FILE_DRAG_ENTER, _MOTION,
                                   _LEAVE or _DROP; uris on drop only

and wpe_view_file_drag() for the platforms to emit it; it tells them
whether anything handles the signal, and a view nothing handles refuses
the drag. The engine does nothing else with a drop: the application
decides what it means (it can, for instance, dispatch drag events into
the page).
Only text/uri-list is taken, and only as a copy, never a move (a move
makes the source delete what it gave).

- Wayland: the clipboard's wl_data_device. An offer is now held apart
  until the selection or enter event says what it is, so a drag no longer
  replaces the clipboard's offer. The URI list is read without blocking.
- X11 (patch 2004): XDND version 5 on top-level windows: XdndAware,
  XdndStatus with XdndActionCopy, the URI list from XdndSelection, then
  XdndFinished.

